PRIVATE REFLECTION: {Core statute: ESA s.67.2 (Bill 27, eff. 25 Oct 2021) voids non-competes for provincially regulated employees hired on/after that date; narrow exceptions only for true C-suite “executives” or sale-of-business. None of A/B/D/E qualify as executives.  
Key split: (1) C is federally regulated (Schedule 1 bank → Canada Labour Code), so ESA ban does not apply and common-law reasonableness test governs → enforceable clause still possible. (2) E (2019 hire) predates ban, so any clause already in original agreement is not statutorily voided. (3) B (lawyer) argued by some on fiduciary/client-duty grounds, but no statutory carve-out exists for that role.  
Consensus leans C (federal jurisdiction trumps); E and B have vocal but minority support. Unresolved: exact wording of “included in their employment agreement” for pre-2021 hires and scope of fiduciary exception. Need to confirm whether any post-2021 reaffirmation or new clause would be allowed for E.}

