Round 2 reinforces prior split: overwhelming majority (colleagues 1,3,4,6,8,10-12,15,18-20) again selects C with detailed rebuttals—federal jurisdiction (Canada Labour Code) exempts Schedule 1 banks entirely; ESA text contains no professional/fiduciary carve-out; question phrasing (“included” as of Jan 2023) eliminates any E grandfathering. Minority (colleagues 2,5,7,9,13,14,16,17,21) persists on B via fiduciary duties/Law Society overlay for lawyers, but still cites no post-amendment statute or case law; several note that even federal roles remain subject to common-law reasonableness.  
