12.text:
PRIVATE REFLECTION: {Key statutory point unchanged: Ontario ESA s.67.2 (post-Oct 25 2021) voids non-competes for most new/renewed agreements except narrow C-suite executive or sale-of-business exceptions; none of listed roles meet those. Pre-2021 clauses not automatically voided by statute, but question phrasing ("included" as of 2023) precludes adding/reaffirming new ones. Federal undertakings (Canada Labour Code) outside ESA entirely.

Round 2 reinforced strong consensus on C (cols 1,10-12,15,18-20,3,4,6,8): Schedule 1 banks are federal, ESA ban inapplicable, common-law reasonableness governs and a clause can be included/remain valid. Persistent minority (cols 13-14,16-17,2,5,7,9) continues pushing B on fiduciary/lawyer exception; countered repeatedly that ESA contains no professional carve-out and fiduciary status is merely common-law overlay without statutory exemption. E support collapsed further: 2019 hire predates ban but cannot support new inclusion now. A/D remain clearly barred.

Unresolved/minor: potential federal-provincial overlap in bank contracts or exact scope of "executive"; common-law reasonableness test still required for C. Current position: C is definitively strongest answer.}

